+
+## Notes on the change
+
+- `from_file()` gets a new keyword-only-style parameter `text: bool = True`. The file is opened with `open(filename, "r" if text else "rb")`, so `text=False` yields a binary-mode handle. `text=True` keeps the previous behavior, so this is backward compatible.
+- The new `test_config_from_file_binary` test verifies the handle is genuinely binary by asserting `fp.read()` returns `bytes`, so it will fail if the mode logic regresses.
+- `tests/static/config.json` doesn't need any changes; the binary test reuses it.
+
+## Running the relevant tests
+
+```shell
+pytest tests/test_config.py
+```
+
+To run only the `from_file` related tests:
+
+```shell
+pytest tests/test_config.py -k from_file
+```
